{"step_index":274,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T03:09:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:09:24+09:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:09:27+09:00\nThe search for \"\"pubcUserNo\" hometax\" returned the following summary:\nIn the context of the Hometax system—specifically when interacting with its **Business Registration Status Inquiry (사업자등록상태조회)** API—`pubcUserNo` is a field used in the XML payload[1][2][3].\n\n### Key Information:\n*   **Purpose:** It is an element within the request map (typically `<map id=\"ATTABZAA001R08\">`) sent to the Hometax server to query the status of a business registration number[2][3][4].\n*   **Usage in API Requests:** In most technical implementations for business status verification, this field is left **empty** (`<pubcUserNo/>`)[1][2][5]. It does not typically require a specific value to be provided by the user for standard public status inquiries[3][4].\n*   **Technical Context:** It appears as a parameter alongside other fields such as `txprDscmNo` (the business registration number) and `dongCode` (an internal processing code)[1][2][4].\n\nIf you are developing an application to check business registration status, you can generally include `<pubcUserNo/>` as an empty tag in your XML request body without needing to populate it with specific user data[3][5][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [tistory.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFBgsA9_ayFqtAu5q0dwoKhQ62GchsQ9E46i3afEfGVKNpebdg-Nk0u2eKVpy7tlcAFcZ6Lcu5XgTooiRIpnfkObUHswc3Ln4zMEv8Se0J7qBmUVag=)\n[2] [tistory.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFOCYqNFfXYNjsQ3WqP-6OWxTRRRk2Er_lxsafMlqZMC40ApZRil6Qg1g-w1OWFVcmaHQ-r7kqzIjG3Ud0o8-MhchGR5pEk5Tgd3jFMmQP9AQhq)\n[3] [tistory.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGE1xUwiQZAHbvm7bnHPVQvHU5_PZLiBjl_QRJXCJQv8jIuOUQ98Zl9MBtU2yQih6aEUlY807-DpTKEnSkhAC16TDA168l-5Q2LRc1SlgtM330=)\n[4] [tistory.com]